&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Xendit, we are looking for a Customer Success Manager (CSM) to support our Greater China clients and help drive their success on our platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the post-go-live customer lifecycle for a portfolio of English- and Mandarin-speaking accounts, working closely with clients to drive product adoption, resolve day-to-day issues, and capture opportunities for growth. You will build a solid understanding of your clients&#39; payment flows and business needs, and use that understanding to make practical recommendations that improve their business outcome and end-customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with both technical and business stakeholders, supporting solutioning discussions and coordinating with Product, Engineering, and Commercial teams to problem solve and address client needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone earlier in their Customer Success career who has a working knowledge of payments and alternative payment methods in Southeast Asia, and is comfortable managing client relationships in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or related client-facing roles within B2B SaaS, fintech, or payments environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments and alternative payment methods (APMs) across Southeast Asia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing client accounts, including driving product adoption, commercial growth &amp;amp; retention, and day-to-day relationship management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage confidently with client stakeholders (managers and product/technical leads)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of technical products (e.g. APIs, integrations, payment flows) and ability to explain product capabilities to clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills in English and Mandarin (business proficiency required in both languages) to support Greater China clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in problem-solving and critical thinking, with a proactive, analytical and detail-oriented approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience supporting clients in Greater China (Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to multi-market or cross-border client environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data analysis or reporting (e.g. transaction success rates)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually curious with a growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of English- and Mandarin-speaking accounts, driving product adoption, commercial growth &amp;amp; retention, and day-to-day relationship management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an understanding of clients&#39; business models and payment flows to identify improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, product knowledge and business understanding to drive and capture portfolio expansion opportunities (upsell, cross-sell, new use cases) in partnership with Account Management and Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a day-to-day point of contact for client stakeholders on product usage and issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage solutioning discussions for new use cases, working with Product and Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor key performance metrics (e.g. payment success rates, payment volume growth, payment method adoption) and flag issues proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively mitigate risks and escalate issues as appropriate to drive high customer satisfaction and optimize Xendit net revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Risk, and Commercial teams to solve pain points and unlock opportunities with clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

