&lt;li&gt;Working experience on reconciliation tools and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own &amp;amp; execute reconciliations for Xendit’s day-to-day financial operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the reconciliation process for all Xendit products across the region, ensuring that all funds are moving as expected and Xendit does not have any exposure or incorrect transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the product teams on automating recons across products and the region to ensure no gaps in the process and Xendit is protected against money loss&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the opportunity to learn how Xendit operates from the ground up and make a real impact on the future of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate with internal and external stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve for unreconciled transactions by working with product, partnerships and finance to identify and resolve root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set up recons for any new products&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As new products are launched and we expand to new markets, set up and own the reconciliation processes to ensure that at all points, Xendit recons are operating at best in class standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do whatever it takes to make Xendit succeed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a strategic and commercially minded &lt;strong&gt;Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to grow a portfolio of high-potential accounts across Southeast Asia and Greater China. You will work with ambitious businesses, including emerging international e-commerce brands and local technology companies, to identify opportunities and support their expansion. We aren&#39;t looking for a &quot;check-in&quot; person, we need a growth architect who thrives on seeing their clients level up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of B2B account management or strategic sales experience in financial services, fintech, or payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently growing revenue within accounts. Experience managing global accounts is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Philippines market, as well as the broader regional landscape, is essential. You understand the needs and cultural nuances of local and cross-border merchants across Southeast Asia and Greater China.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder &amp;amp; Founder-Like Mentality: You thrive in “zero-to-one” environments. You are hands-on, take full ownership, and are relentless in removing blockers for your clients and your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional Communicator: You possess professional proficiency in English. You can persuasively present to local and cross-border merchant stakeholders in the Philippines and across Southeast Asia and Greater China, and collaborate effectively with internal teams Globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Led &amp;amp; Analytical: You make decisions based on data, not gut feel. You can analyze transaction patterns to identify untapped potential and risks merchant may face&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attributes We Value:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hustle with Integrity: You move fast, but you build trust through transparency and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity: You constantly ask “why” and dig deep to understand the root problem, not just the surface request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience: You are undeterred by long sales cycles and complex procurement processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.⁠ ⁠ Portfolio Growth &amp;amp; Revenue Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full P&amp;amp;L for a portfolio of accounts. Drive revenue and transaction volume through upselling, cross-selling (payment acceptance, FX, payouts) and new use case expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive 12-18 month account plans for each major client, articulating clear growth strategies and proactively managing churn risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently exceed revenue targets by focusing on high-impact input metrics and maintaining a clean, accurate pipeline in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2.⁠ ⁠Executive &amp;amp; Multi-Stakeholder Relationship Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture C-level relationships (CEO, CFO, Head of Product, CTO) within your accounts. Understand their strategic objectives and align Xendit’s roadmap to solve their core business challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) and executive business reviews, providing data-driven insights and demonstrating clear ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the trusted advisor and single point of contact, navigating complex organizational structures to secure buy-in and consensus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.⁠ ⁠Cross-Functional Influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal teams (Product, Marketing, Engineering, Compliance, Legal) to bring the our clients’ needs back to the organization, influencing our product roadmap and regional strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Account Executive and Customer Success teams to identify and scope net-new opportunities, bridging the gap between commercial terms and technical feasibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4.⁠ ⁠Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Local Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of regulatory shifts and payment trends in Southeast Asia. Act as a subject matter expert on cross-border flows between&amp;nbsp; Southeast Asia and CN/HK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify synergies between Xendit’s 7-market licensed infrastructure and the specific needs of the Philippines expanding into the region and vice versa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do whatever it takes to make Xendit succeed!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Xendit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impact at Scale: You won’t be a small cog in a giant machine. You will own a significant book of business that directly impacts Xendit’s regional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensed Infrastructure: Sell more than just a gateway. You have acquiring, remittance , banking, VASP, and lending licenses as your arsenal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture of Builders: We are a team of doers. We hire people who want to build, not just maintain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerated Career Growth: We promote from within and offer high-visibility projects with direct exposure to global leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Role Purpose&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MLRO is the appointed Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing (AML/CFT) officer responsible for the design, implementation and ongoing effectiveness of Xendit Thailand&#39;s AML/CFT, sanctions and financial crime compliance framework. The role acts as the primary liaison with the Anti-Money Laundering Office (AMLO), law enforcement agencies and other regulators e.g. Bank of Thailand (BOT).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Office Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TH operations Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the appointed MLRO and maintain overall accountability for the AML/CFT framework and a point of contact to AMLO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement and continuously enhance AML/CFT, sanctions, fraud and financial crime policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform enterprise-wide AML/CFT risk assessments and ensure mitigating controls remain effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regulatory inspections, audits and information requests from AMLO and other authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide AML/CFT advisory support for new products including payment gateway, direct acquiring, payment orchestration, payouts, remittance (where applicable), QR payments and cross-border services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare AML/CFT MI reports, KRIs and Board/Management Committee reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead remediation actions arising from audits, regulatory reviews and internal assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop &amp;amp; Oversight AML/CFT training programmes and foster a strong compliance culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for AML reporting &amp;amp; support BOT regulatory reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Customer Due Diligence (CDD), Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD), ongoing monitoring and customer risk rating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle escalations from the Merchant Operations (MO) team regarding onboarding of merchants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle name-screening escalations from L1 analysts during real-time monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle escalations from L1 analysts during post-transaction monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review STR investigations escalated from L1 analysts and prepare Suspicious Transaction Reports (STRs) and regulatory filings to AMLO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern sanctions screening (customer and transaction), adverse media screening, and PEP reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Key Qualifications&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Law, Finance, Business, Risk Management, Compliance or related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years&#39; experience in AML/CFT, financial crime compliance or regulatory compliance within banks, payment service providers, fintech or financial institutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging directly with AMLO or other financial regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the Payment Systems Act, AMLO AML/CFT requirements, sanctions obligations and relevant international standards (FATF).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certification such as ACAMS, ICA or equivalent is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong regulatory judgement and risk management mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially minded while maintaining regulatory independence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced fintech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity and sound ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Authority&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MLRO has authority to escalate material AML/CFT issues directly, Head of Compliance, senior management and the Board, request information from all business units, require remediation of AML/CFT control weaknesses, and independently determine STR filing decisions in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Regulatory References&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anti-Money Laundering Act B.E. 2542 (as amended)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant AMLO Notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bank of Thailand regulations applicable to Payment Service Providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FATF Recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a technically-minded, client-facing Senior Solutions Engineer to join our regional/global go to market team. In this role, you will be the bridge between our enterprise clients and Xendit&#39;s product/engineering teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner directly with our Account Executives and Account Managers to drive the technical win in complex sales cycles. You will listen to client needs, architect payment solutions across Xendit&#39;s 7-market licensed infrastructure, and guide clients from initial technical discovery through to successful integration and launch. This is a presales advisory role focused on deal velocity and technical credibility&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Technical Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in a client-facing technical role, preferably in payments, fintech, or SaaS (e.g., Solutions Engineer, Sales Engineer, Solutions Architect, Integration Consultant).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of APIs, webhooks, and SDKs. You can read code samples and explain technical concepts to engineers—even if you don&#39;t code daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment flows, acquiring, FX, and/or payouts is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with regional/global enterprise clients is essential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Fluency: You bridge the gap between business and engineering. You can whiteboard a solution architecture, troubleshoot API calls, and translate technical capabilities into business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-Facing Presence: You are comfortable presenting to CTOs and lead engineers, handling objections with confidence, and building trust with technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-Solving Mindset: You don&#39;t just answer questions—you uncover underlying needs and propose creative, compliant solutions across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel Flexibility: Willingness to travel for client meetings and internal alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes We Value&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder Mentality: You thrive in &quot;zero-to-one&quot; environments and enjoy rolling up your sleeves to solve ambiguous problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity: You constantly ask &quot;why&quot; and dig deep to understand client businesses, not just their technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility &amp;amp; Collaboration: You know that the best solutions come from teamwork—internally with sales, product, and engineering, and externally with clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively in Mandarin (spoken and written) is advantageous to conduct technical presentations, support presales activities, and build relationships with Mandarin-speaking clients and partners across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.⁠ ⁠Technical Pre-Sales Solution Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⁠Partner with the regional/global sales team to understand prospect needs and design tailored payment solutions leveraging Xendit&#39;s full product suite (acquiring, FX, payouts, stablecoin remittances).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct technical discovery sessions with prospective clients (CTOs, Heads of Product, Lead Engineers) to map their infrastructure and identify integration requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect solutions that address complex cross-border flows between regional/global and Southeast Asia, ensuring compliance and optimal commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling product demonstrations and technical presentations to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2.⁠ ⁠RFP / RFI Support &amp;amp; Technical Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical response for RFPs and RFIs from regional/global enterprise clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare solution diagrams, integration guides, and technical proposal documents that clearly articulate Xendit&#39;s value proposition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with legal and compliance teams to address technical and regulatory questions during the sales cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.⁠ ⁠Proof of Concept (POC) &amp;amp; Integration Advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and manage technical proof of concepts (POCs) for complex enterprise opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide clients through sandbox testing and integration planning, reducing time-to-go-live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the trusted technical advisor during the sales process, building confidence in Xendit&#39;s platform and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4.⁠ ⁠Voice of the Customer to Product&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture and synthesize client feedback, technical requirements, and feature requests to share with Xendit&#39;s product and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of competitor solutions and market trends regionally/globally - SEA payments corridor, providing insights to inform product roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal knowledge bases, playbooks, and enablement materials for the broader commercial team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5.⁠ ⁠Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Account Executives to develop account strategies and identify upsell/cross-sell opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Success and Integration teams to ensure smooth handoffs and long-term client satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global Solutions Engineering peers to share best practices and scalable solution patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do whatever it takes to make Xendit succeed!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;We are looking for an experienced Product Director to lead our core payment portfolios,&lt;/span&gt; encompassing &lt;strong&gt;Payments Acceptance (Cards &amp;amp; LPMs) and Payouts.&lt;/strong&gt; In this role, you will define the long-term product vision, set the strategic roadmap, and drive the evolution of our B2B payments infrastructure. We are seeking a visionary product leader who has a deep understanding of the payments industry, knows what best-in-class looks like, and can elevate our product offerings to deliver scalable, high-performing solutions across multiple regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;What you’ll do in this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,0,0&quot;&gt;Define and own the long-term product strategy and comprehensive roadmaps for large-scale payment portfolios, focusing on future growth and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,1,0&quot;&gt;Drive product performance and take ownership of key commercial and technical metrics, including authorization/success rates, total payment volume (TPV), cost of acceptance, and margin optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,2,0&quot;&gt;Build and scale robust B2B payment products and infrastructure across multiple regions and complex regulatory jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,3,0&quot;&gt;Partner closely with engineering teams, utilizing your technical background to guide how payment systems, connections, and integrations work together seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,4,0&quot;&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a high-performing team of Product Managers and Senior Product Managers, fostering a culture of strategic thinking paired with hands-on product ownership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;What you’ll need in this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,0,0&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience in Product Management, with a proven track record of leading product teams and owning end-to-end strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,1,0&quot;&gt;Deep knowledge of card acquiring and/or local payment methods, specifically gained from working at a Payment Service Provider (PSP) or a dedicated payments technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,2,0&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience building and managing large B2B payment portfolios rather than just individual features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,3,0&quot;&gt;Highly metrics-minded and analytical, with direct experience managing payments economics and performance indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,4,0&quot;&gt;Technical fluency necessary to understand and navigate complex payment architectures and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;4,5,0&quot;&gt;Preferred: Experience with payouts/disbursements, Southeast Asia or emerging market payment methods (e-wallets, QR, etc.), multi-acquirer routing, and fraud/risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Why this role exists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a payment-infrastructure company, the product is in large part the API. Developers are both the buyers and the daily users, and the quality of the APIs, SDKs, docs, sandbox, and integration path is the product&#39;s real surface. This role owns the developer&#39;s journey from first API call to production and scale, the difference between a developer who integrates in an afternoon and one who gives up before their first successful transaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The roadmap for the developer experience:&lt;/strong&gt; integration flow, SDKs, documentation, sandbox, error handling, and time-to-first-successful-call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer activation and retention&lt;/strong&gt; as headline metrics, from sign-up to first production transaction and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery grounded in developer behavior:&lt;/strong&gt; integration analytics, support and community signals, and direct developer research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership with Engineering &lt;/strong&gt;on API design and DX standards, and prioritization of DX debt against new capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communication of trade-offs&lt;/strong&gt; to senior stakeholders, and translation of platform changes into a coherent developer-facing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How you will work&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You report to the Product Design &amp;amp; UX Director for Customer Lifecycle and work most closely with Engineering, whose API and platform decisions shape the experience you own. Part of your early work is helping define where developer-experience ownership sits, since this surface has not had a dedicated product owner before. You are the strategic owner of the developer journey from first API call to production. Your time splits between developer discovery and roadmap delivery, with constant engineering partnership. The domain works from validated findings rather than assumptions and values direct, candid critique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PM experience with API, platform, or developer-facing products.&lt;/strong&gt; You have owned products where developers are the user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genuine technical fluency. &lt;/strong&gt;You can read API docs and discuss schemas, auth, and webhooks with engineers, here this is a requirement, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated empathy for developer workflows. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand how developers actually work and where they get stuck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong plus: a background as a developer, or having built SDK, docs, or DX products; payments or fintech experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially minded, forward-thinking Regulatory Compliance and AML Manager to help shape the next phase of Xendit&#39;s growth in Singapore. This is an opportunity to go beyond traditional compliance oversight and play a meaningful role in building the regulatory infrastructure that enables a fast-growing payments business to scale responsibly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will take ownership of key regulatory and financial crime compliance responsibilities in Singapore, working closely with senior leadership, Product, Engineering, Risk and Commercial teams to translate complex regulatory requirements into practical, scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines deep regulatory expertise with strong systems thinking — someone who can navigate ambiguity, challenge existing processes and build frameworks that are both regulator-ready and operationally efficient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership individual contributor role with significant cross-functional exposure and the opportunity to develop into broader functional or regional leadership as the business evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree-holder with minimum 7+ years of experience in regulatory compliance, AML/CFT or financial crime risk management within regulated financial services, payments or fintech.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of AML/CFT frameworks, customer due diligence, transaction monitoring, sanctions screening and financial crime risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong recent and working knowledge of Singapore&#39;s regulatory environment, including MAS requirements applicable to licensed Major Payment Institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self-motivation and a proactive approach to problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound commercial judgment, with the ability to balance regulatory requirements, risk appetite and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate complex regulatory requirements into practical operational controls and sustainable processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with experience influencing cross-functional teams and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating independently in a fast-moving environment, taking ownership of complex problems from ambiguity through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management and organizational skills to prioritize effectively in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing or working with transaction monitoring systems and compliance tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth fintech, payments infrastructure company or technology-led financial services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of building, scaling or transforming compliance frameworks, particularly in environments experiencing rapid growth or organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment acceptance, acquiring, cross-border payments, payouts, e-money or platform-based payment models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Product, Engineering or Data teams to design or improve technology-enabled compliance controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to compliance automation, RegTech, AI-enabled workflows or transaction monitoring systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across multiple APAC jurisdictions or supporting regional regulatory initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certifications such as CAMS, ICA or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Regulatory Compliance &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously strengthen operational and procedural adherence to applicable MAS requirements, including the Payment Services Act (PSA), Financial Services and Markets Act (FSMA), relevant MAS Notices (e.g., PSN01, PSN02, PSN03) and other applicable notices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regulatory engagement including license-related matters&amp;nbsp; regulatory applications and variations, and ongoing submissions and supervisory examinations, serving as a trusted point of contact for&amp;nbsp; the MAS and other relevant authorities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate, interpret, and assess regulatory developments in Singapore and the broader APAC region, translating regulatory changes into actionable business, product and operational requirements for internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a risk-based approach to regulatory governance, ensuring robust controls, clear accountability and effective oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Financial Crime Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and enhance Xendit’s AML/CFT compliance framework, ensuring alignment with local statutory obligations and international regulatory standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee enhanced due diligence (EDD), transaction monitoring, sanctions screening, periodic reviews and suspicious transaction reporting operational workflows, maintaining dynamic rules, identifying weaknesses in existing controls and driving sustainable and timely remediation through improved policies, processes and technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply sound judgment to complex merchant and transaction risk assessments, balancing regulatory expectations with commercial realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with operational teams to improve the effectiveness, efficiency and scalability of financial crime controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Scalable Compliance Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate regulatory obligations into scalable operating processes, technology-enabled controls and governance frameworks that support increasing transaction volumes and business complexity Partner with Product, Engineering and Operations to embed compliance requirements into product architecture, merchant onboarding and payment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, update, and implement local compliance policies, standard operating procedures (SOPs), and governance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver localized AML/CFT frameworks that can be adapted across products to foster a high-standard compliance culture across all local operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic compliance partner to Product, Commercial and senior leadership teams on new products, partnerships and complex enterprise merchant requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Bonus Compliance Superpower&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who brings more than deep regulatory and AML/CFT expertise. Ideally, you have a second area of technical specialization that sets you apart! Whether that&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a deep understanding of payments infrastructure and fund flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;hands-on experience with compliance engineering and RegTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;expertise in data analytics and financial crime detection,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the ability to translate regulatory requirements into product architecture and technology-enabled controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience building transaction monitoring systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;lead complex licensing initiatives across multiple markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;or automated compliance processes at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We don&#39;t expect you to have all these capabilities. What excites us is someone who combines strong regulatory foundations with a distinctive technical skill set, and wants to apply both to building the next generation of compliance infrastructure at Xendit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why join Xendit?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build, don&#39;t just maintain&lt;/strong&gt;. Help shape the compliance infrastructure of a growing payments platform, with the opportunity to solve complex regulatory challenges through technology and better systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work at the intersection of regulation and innovation&lt;/strong&gt;. Partner directly with the teams building payment products and infrastructure used by leading businesses across Southeast Asia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have meaningful ownership and influence&lt;/strong&gt;. Take responsibility for critical regulatory outcomes, influence business decisions and work closely with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow into broader leadership&lt;/strong&gt;. Develop the experience, relationships and track record to pursue future opportunities in functional leadership, regional compliance or larger transformation initiatives as the organization scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and proactive Regulatory Compliance and AML Manager to join our team in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. In this independent contributor role, you will be the driving force behind ensuring our company&#39;s adherence to all relevant Malaysia regulations, internal policies, and ethical standards. You will identify and address compliance needs autonomously, taking initiative to conduct risk assessments, investigations, and training initiatives. Reporting to Regional Compliance, this role demands a self-directed individual who thrives in a fast-paced environment and takes ownership of their responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Law, Management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10 years of experience in AML and regulatory compliance, preferably in the FinTech space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in front-facing financial services regulators in Malaysia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the central bank (Bank Negara Malaysia, BNM) regulations, AML/CFT requirements, and cross-border payment frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory licensing processes and engagement with supervisory authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self-motivation and a proactive approach to problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently and take ownership of your tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management and organizational skills to prioritize effectively in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with minimal supervision and seek guidance only when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing or working with transaction monitoring systems and compliance tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Compliance &amp;amp; Licensing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with BNM regulations, including merchant acquiring and planned cross-border activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the licensing application process for new regulatory approvals, working closely with internal stakeholders and regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and interpret regulatory developments, ensuring timely implementation of changes in laws and guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison with BNM and other relevant regulatory bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AML/CFT &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the AML/CFT compliance programme, ensuring adherence to local and international standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement risk-based approaches to transaction monitoring, customer due diligence (CDD), and enhanced due diligence (EDD) for high-risk customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure robust sanctions screening processes are in place, aligned with regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct compliance testing and assessments, identifying gaps and ensuring timely remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Advisory &amp;amp; Business Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide proactive compliance guidance to business teams on new product launches, partnerships, and commercial initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of internal policies and procedures, ensuring they align with regulatory expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compliance training to internal teams, fostering a strong compliance culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage regulatory reporting obligations, ensuring timely and accurate submissions to BNM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance the compliance monitoring framework, ensuring effective oversight of business activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with regional compliance teams to harmonise best practices across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Xendit, we are looking for a Senior Implementations Manager&amp;nbsp;to lead the successful onboarding of large mainland Chinese enterprise clients onto our payments platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the end-to-end implementation journey — from post-sale handover through to go-live — ensuring clients are set up for long-term success. You will work closely with customers to understand their business models, payment flows, and operational requirements, translating these into structured implementation plans and technical integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage complex onboarding projects involving API integrations, payment method configuration, and system alignment with clients’ internal processes. This includes coordinating across internal teams (Sales, Product, Engineering, Compliance) and external client stakeholders to drive timely and high-quality delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the primary point of contact during onboarding, you will proactively manage timelines, risks, and dependencies, while maintaining clear and consistent communication with clients — including enterprise stakeholders in Greater China. You will also guide clients through best practices, provide enablement and training, and ensure a smooth transition to post go-live ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who combines strong project management discipline with client-facing experience in complex B2B or fintech environments, and is comfortable operating in fast-paced, high-growth settings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–6 years of experience in onboarding, implementation, professional services, or project management roles within B2B SaaS, fintech, or payments environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading end-to-end enterprise implementations, from post-sale handover through to go-live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management capabilities, including experience managing timelines, dependencies, risks, and multiple stakeholders across concurrent projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with APIs, system integrations, or technical product implementations (ability to work closely with engineering teams and translate technical concepts to clients)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage and manage enterprise clients, including handling complex requirements, escalations, and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Compliance teams to deliver client outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills in English and Mandarin (business proficiency required) to effectively support Greater China clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of ownership and accountability, with the ability to operate independently in fast-paced, high-growth environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure, particularly working with APIs, payment flows, or regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience supporting or onboarding enterprise clients in Greater China (Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in consulting, system integration, or professional services, with exposure to structured project delivery methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with project management frameworks (e.g. Agile, Scrum, or Waterfall) and tools (e.g. Jira, Asana, Notion)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multi-market or cross-border implementations, including navigating regulatory, operational, or cultural nuances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth or fast-scaling technology companies, with the ability to adapt processes and operate in evolving environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to data migration, system mapping, or workflow design as part of client onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving mindset with the ability to identify process gaps and proactively improve implementation playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end onboarding and implementation for enterprise and mid-market clients, from post-sale handover through to successful go-live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage structured implementation plans, including timelines, milestones, dependencies, and clear success criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact during onboarding, building strong relationships with client stakeholders and driving alignment across technical and business teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical integrations, working closely with clients and internal engineering teams on API implementation, system configuration, and workflow alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage risks, issues, and escalations, ensuring blockers are identified early and resolved efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, Risk, and Compliance teams to deliver high-quality onboarding outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate client workshops, solution discussions, and training sessions to ensure successful product adoption and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clear and consistent communication, including regular status updates, stakeholder reporting, and executive-level summaries where required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding of Greater China enterprise clients, navigating language, cultural, and operational nuances effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously identify opportunities to improve onboarding processes, tooling, and playbooks, contributing to scaling the OIM function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth handover to post-go-live teams (e.g. Customer Success / Account Management), with clear documentation and context transfer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Xendit, we are seeking a Senior Product Manager - Cards to help shape and scale our card acquiring product. You will join our growing cards team, working closely with our existing Cards product lead and reporting to the Product Director, Payments Acceptance. In this role, you will own card acquiring initiatives end to end, from authorisation and processing flows to connections with acquirers and card schemes, and help define our acquiring strategy, including licensing and acquirer partnerships. You will also work to improve authorisation rates and manage chargebacks and settlement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, or a strong track record in card products, with a strong focus on execution and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on card acquiring experience, ideally at a card acquirer processing Visa and Mastercard transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently own card acquiring initiatives from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to understand how payment systems work together (e.g. APIs, authorisation and settlement flows)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple regions and regulatory jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-minded, having owned key metrics for your product area (e.g. authorisation rate, TPV, margin)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building B2B products or integrating B2B offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching global products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear understanding of card economics (e.g. interchange, scheme fees, acquiring margin)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with card schemes (Visa, Mastercard) from the acquirer side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with card licensing or connecting to new acquirers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve card acquiring and processing flows, including authorisation, capture and refunds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and expand Xendit&#39;s connections to acquirers and card schemes (Visa, Mastercard)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Xendit&#39;s acquiring strategy, including licensing and acquirer partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve authorisation rates and manage chargeback and settlement performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own key metrics for your area, such as authorisation rate, TPV and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend time with merchants to understand their card payment needs and turn them into clear product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Risk, Finance and commercial teams to deliver card products on time and to a high standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Xendit, we are seeking a Senior Product Manager - Payments Acceptance (Merchant of Record) who will build, launch, and scale Xendit&#39;s new Merchant of Record (MoR) offering across cards and local payment methods, starting in Southeast Asia and expanding to global markets. In this role, you will take full ownership of end-to-end payment acceptance flows, managing complex liabilities around local entity compliance, tax withholding, cross-border FX settlement, and chargeback mitigation for global enterprise merchants. Working at the intersection of product, engineering, risk, legal, and commercial teams, you will take this product from 0 to 1 and scale it to deliver seamless checkout conversion while maintaining airtight compliance rails across high-throughput transaction environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience in fintech, payment gateways, card acquiring, or B2B payment platforms, or an equivalent proven track record with MoR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with the Merchant of Record (MoR) model (must-have), either from the provider side (e.g. building or running an MoR or managed payments product) or from the merchant side (e.g. working at a company that used MoR services to process payments locally and settle cross-border).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency with RESTful APIs, webhooks, sandbox testing environments, and financial data reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating regulatory, tax, and compliance requirements across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills with hands-on capability to query data independently, optimize unit economics, and define clear product metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing cross-border payments, localized FX solutions, or global merchant acquirers across global markets (e.g. Asia, Latin America, Africa, or Europe).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-scale tech startups, e-commerce infrastructure platforms, or global SaaS scale-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience partnering with card schemes, acquirers, and local payment method operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building zero-to-one product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product strategy and roadmap for Xendit&#39;s new Merchant of Record (MoR) acceptance offering, from the 0-to-1 launch across cards and local payment methods to expansion into new markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and launch end-to-end MoR payment flows that let global merchants accept payments locally without having a local entity: collecting in local currency, handling FX and local tax, and settling cross-border in the merchant&#39;s currency, starting with cards and extending to local payment methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to build MoR capabilities on top of Xendit&#39;s existing acceptance stack of 100+ payment methods and connections, including reliable APIs and automated settlement and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Legal, Compliance, Tax, Finance, and Risk to define how Xendit takes on the liabilities of being the Merchant of Record in each market, including local tax, regulatory requirements, chargebacks, and fraud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend time with merchants and prospects to understand their problems and why they need to process locally without a local presence, and consult stakeholders across the business before proposing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own success metrics for the MoR product, such as merchant adoption, Total Payment Volume (TPV) processed through MoR, transaction success rate, and margin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear PRDs and acceptance criteria, and work with Go-To-Market (GTM) and Customer Success teams to launch MoR to enterprise merchants and support their onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Product Manager to drive the next generation of XenPlatform. XenPlatform is one of the most complex products in Xendit’s payment processing stack. Your main job will be to set its overall product direction and make sure we can serve marketplaces and platforms across all our regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond long-term strategy, we need someone who can get into the weeds and break complex problems down for our engineering teams. You’ll bring payments experience, a track record of building global products at scale, and strong commercial judgement, so that what we build covers all our markets and scales sustainably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have full ownership of your team’s strategy, priorities and outcomes, and the autonomy to define the next phase of XenPlatform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do in this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the overall product strategy and roadmap, balancing competing stakeholder requests across teams and clearly communicating your prioritisation framework to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand enterprise customers across segments (marketplaces, embedded finance and SaaS platforms), leveraging their feedback to define your longer-term roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Compliance, Legal and GTM to define the ideal customer profile (ICP) Xendit should focus on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design intuitive experiences across the API and the Xendit Dashboard, so merchants can clearly see how their platforms are performing and accurately reconcile their own data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable account structures that accurately reflect how our enterprise merchants’ organisations are set up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Design to deliver products and features on time and to a high standard, making sure every XenPlatform feature is on par with or better than what’s in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll need in this role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience in fintech and/or B2B products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments processing (acquiring/issuing) or cross-border payouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with onboarding and KYC/KYB flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving roadmap and execution across cross-functional teams, owning north-star metrics such as TPV, conversion or retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the technical, regulatory and operational challenges of building global financial products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, concise communication style that adapts to your audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and comfort using data to understand customer behaviour and make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen, with the judgement to balance commercial and product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and strategically-minded Account Manager to own and grow our regional/global enterprise portfolio, based in our Jakarta office, working in a hybrid model. This position is dedicated to our most complex and high-value enterprise clients — primarily cross-border e-commerce leaders, global SaaS platforms, and large-scale financial institutions across Indonesia and the wider APAC region. You’ll join Xendit’s Enterprise Account Management team, working closely with Go-to-Market, Product, Engineering, Compliance, Legal, Operations and Risk leadership. You will not just manage accounts — you will architect growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of B2B account management or strategic sales experience in financial services, fintech, or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent track record of meeting or exceeding revenue targets, ideally in a role with direct P&amp;amp;L, book-of-business, or portfolio revenue ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and growing revenue within large and complex enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the needs of international cross-border merchants and the cultural nuances of doing business across APAC markets. Familiarity with the APAC region is essential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in both English and Bahasa Indonesia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder &amp;amp; Founder-Like Mentality: You thrive in “zero-to-one” environments. You are hands-on, take full ownership, and are relentless in removing blockers for your clients and your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional Communicator: You can present persuasively in the boardroom, and translate complex payment concepts for executive audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Led &amp;amp; Analytical: You make decisions based on data, not gut feel. You can analyze transaction patterns to identify risk and untapped potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attributes We Value:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hustle with Integrity: You move fast, but you build trust through transparency and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity: You constantly ask “why” and dig deep to understand the root problem, not just the surface request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience: You are undeterred by long sales cycles and complex procurement processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1.⁠ ⁠Strategic Portfolio Growth &amp;amp; Revenue Ownership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full P&amp;amp;L for a portfolio of key enterprise accounts. Drive revenue and transaction volume through upselling, cross-selling (payment acceptance, payouts, platform business) and use case expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive 12-18 month account plans for each major client, articulating clear growth strategies and proactively managing churn risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently exceed revenue targets by focusing on high-impact input metrics and maintaining a clean, accurate pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2.⁠ ⁠Executive &amp;amp; Multi-Stakeholder Relationship Building&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture C-level relationships (CEO, CFO, CPO, CTO) within your accounts. Understand their strategic objectives and align Xendit’s roadmap to solve their core business challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client business reviews, providing data-driven insights and demonstrating clear ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the trusted advisor and single point of contact, navigating complex organizational structures to secure client buy-in and consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3.⁠ ⁠Cross-Functional Influence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring your clients’ needs back to Xendit, informing and influencing our product roadmap and strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams (Product, Solution Engineering, Compliance, Legal, Risk) to identify and scope net-new opportunities, bridging the gap between commercial terms and technical feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4.⁠ ⁠Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Local Expertise&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of regulatory shifts and payment trends. Act as a subject matter expert on cross-border flows between Xendit markets in APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify synergies between Xendit’s licensed infrastructure and the specific needs of enterprises expanding into the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Xendit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impact at Scale: You won’t be a small cog in a giant machine. You will own a significant book of business that directly impacts Xendit’s regional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensed Infrastructure: Sell more than just a gateway. You have acquiring, remittance , banking, VASP, and lending licenses as your arsenal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture of Builders: We are a team of doers. We hire people who want to build, not just maintain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerated Career Growth: We promote from within and offer high-visibility projects with direct exposure to global leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Xendit is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to building an inclusive team where everyone can do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Why this role exists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This domain runs on trade-offs, experience versus compliance, merchant versus developer, and those decisions are better made with evidence than with opinion. This role owns generative and evaluative research across the merchant lifecycle and the developer experience, and makes research a standing input to how the domain prioritizes rather than an occasional favor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The research roadmap across the domain&#39;s three clusters&lt;/strong&gt;, prioritized against the decisions that most need evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mixed methods:&lt;/strong&gt; interviews, usability testing, surveys, and behavioral/funnel analysis in partnership with Data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turning findings into decisions&lt;/strong&gt; PMs and designers act on, influence through evidence rather than authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A lightweight insight repository, &lt;/strong&gt;and a practical model for democratizing good-enough research while protecting rigor on high-stakes questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How you will work&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You report to the Product Design &amp;amp; UX Director for Customer Lifecycle and work across all three clusters, partnering with the PMs and designers who rely on your evidence to prioritize. You set the research cadence and the insight repository, and you decide where rigor matters most and where lightweight research is enough. Much of your impact comes through influence rather than mandate, moving decisions with evidence. The domain works from validated findings rather than assumptions and values direct, candid critique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mixed-methods UX research experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You are fluent across qualitative and quantitative approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ability to translate findings into product decisions&lt;/strong&gt; and to influence without authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigor paired with pragmatism&lt;/strong&gt; on timelines, you know where depth matters and where speed is enough.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong plus:&lt;/strong&gt; fintech/regulated or developer-audience research; quantitative fluency; ResearchOps or repository-building experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.xendit.co/en/&quot;&gt;Xendit&lt;/a&gt; is an enterprise payments platform powering complex financial operations across Southeast Asia and global markets. We provide a unified API layer combining payment processing, global payouts, localized FX, identity compliance, and fraud protection. As a trusted financial partner backed by top-tier global investors, Xendit processes high-throughput transaction flows for leading global platforms including Meta, Traveloka, ByteDance, Wise, and Grab, building resilient payment infrastructure to drive regional commerce forward.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional operational leader to serve as our VP, Customer Success and Support. In this executive role, you will take full ownership of our global Customer Success and Support organizations, shaping the complete merchant lifecycle and driving client retention as our platform expands worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You combine strategic vision, process architecture, domain expertise, and a passion for payments. If you excel at diagnosing operational bottlenecks, collaborating directly with Product teams to fix underlying issues, and bringing focus and pace to ambitious goals, this role offers the platform to transform merchant operations at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Leadership &amp;amp; Team Scaling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a global team: Lead, mentor, and scale Customer Success and Support organizations across multiple countries focused on client outcomes and operational efficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and scale: Think ahead with a data-driven instinct, recognizing patterns early and building the frameworks, workflows and tooling to resolve merchant issues fast and protect retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead through change: Help teams adapt and thrive as the organization grows and priorities evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the merchant’s voice: Turn merchant feedback into clear, thoughtful, requirements for Product and Engineering, driving self-serve capabilities and platform improvements, while prioritizing based on business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk &amp;amp; compliance collaboration: Navigate dynamic regulatory mandates (including AML, KYC, PCI-DSS, and regional financial laws) to keep client management, and success playbooks fully compliant with Risk and Legal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Strategy &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; success measures: Establish, monitor, and optimize core performance indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision making: Leverage quantitative insight to map user journeys, anticipate risk, uncover portfolio expansion opportunities, and continuously elevate baseline targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Strategy &amp;amp; Merchant Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global mindset: Lead support and success teams across multiple countries, adapting strategies to each market’s dynamics and client segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Merchant advocacy: Foster enduring partnerships with key strategic clients and act as the executive sponsor for high-priority accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Questions You May Help Answer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which recurring merchant issues should we eliminate at the source, and what would it take?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How should we measure merchant health so it reliably signals churn risk?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do we resolve merchant issues faster, and make sure they stay resolved?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where should Xendit invest in AI and self-serve to scale support while raising the bar on experience?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do we balance risk and compliance requirements with a seamless merchant experience?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What should our global Customer Success and Support model look like as we bring operations together across regions? What support coverage model will serve merchants across time zones and languages as we scale?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which capabilities should we build in-house, and where should we partner?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do we build the next generation of leaders from within our teams?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How should we tailor our service model for global enterprises versus regional SMEs?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience managing Customer Success and/or Support and scaling leadership across merchant operations, support, or client success within high-growth tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with payment infrastructure, financial technology, or SaaS platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience steering end-to-end processing workflows, spanning authorization, clearing, settlement, payouts, and dispute resolution channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to guide organizations through rapid expansion and operational transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product instinct, with a history of translating operational friction into functional engineering specs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehension of financial compliance, risk controls, and regional regulatory frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous analytical approach to dissecting complex problems and establishing data-driven processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of supporting varied merchant tiers, ranging from SME to global multi-market enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Xendit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is an opportunity to sit at the center of how Xendit&#39;s global Ops organization evolves. You will work directly with the President and Global Head of Product, gain exposure across Xendit&#39;s products and markets, and collaborate with leaders throughout the company. You will see how major decisions are made to achieve operating leverage - and help improve the system through which those decisions become reality. For someone who wants to become an exceptional technology operator or future business leader, few roles offer this combination of breadth, access and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
